k=0.000\\,8,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=200\\,000.$ Therefore, the population is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.000\\,8P(200\\,000-P).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100943 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a4751337-93bf-5b47-8b3f-32100820b19a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Logistic Growth Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29c6621c-2a84-5be7-92b6-7a8d9a34cef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=y(2-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348816} {:answer/id #uuid "2ad50b10-a787-5de2-92ed-747b1d730ff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=2+y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348826} {:answer/id #uuid "465dbfcf-7f46-59e0-9e87-913b6084abf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349087} {:answer/id #uuid "938cb335-4e1f-58de-bf60-7c34ccdd9aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=y(2+y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349765} {:answer/id #uuid "e8389761-f855-5a51-83d5-ab0558106e62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=2-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29c6621c-2a84-5be7-92b6-7a8d9a34cef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=y(2-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348816} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6e90022-ffea-5ad7-b103-9f5780f7dcf8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351143}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91925a6d-d444-5dc5-b5e4-01affa0e79dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-83848" :question/problem "Which of the following differential equations is a logistic growth equation?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFrom the given options, the only logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=y(2-y).\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=1,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100943 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a4751337-93bf-5b47-8b3f-32100820b19a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Logistic Growth Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f22fbf4-e2a1-5430-b987-ad309011b129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=20y-2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447257} {:answer/id #uuid "26312008-2455-55a8-bc1d-9b869b44fda8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=20-2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447259} {:answer/id #uuid "2c745c03-98a8-571c-aa79-f32d40ebf4e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=20+y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447261} {:answer/id #uuid "cf11bce7-e4f3-5e71-8383-6e355495bc3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=20y+2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447281} {:answer/id #uuid "d3fc1100-2d33-56a2-a856-01e2f5f30f90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=20{y}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f22fbf4-e2a1-5430-b987-ad309011b129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=20y-2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447257} :answer-field/id #uuid "17f1684b-41e0-59c7-9d1d-0134c261dee4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "52ad75c1-24f1-5969-9d6c-0ceaa8d872d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-83850" :question/problem "Which of the following differential equations is a logistic growth equation?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFrom the given options, the only logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=20y-2{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTo see this, let's factor the right-hand side of the equation. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=2y(10-y).\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=2,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447296 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100943 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a4751337-93bf-5b47-8b3f-32100820b19a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Logistic Growth Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19c12834-371c-5f63-bdfb-02c2541583fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=5{y}^{2}-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447255} {:answer/id #uuid "1d5f4efc-0abf-57f1-ba32-0185947e100a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=5+y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447256} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2458c3-7905-560b-b228-5e789283c915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=55y-11{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447266} {:answer/id